From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:38:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 54/79] core lanes: opt-in pooled shared budgets, as db281878's
 Rule.budgets allocated them

Model.pooled_budgets (off by default): a shared round's head budgets come from allocate over
the stream chains with the measured overhead (head steps inside it) and max(streams,
batch_rows) rows, and no rotating probe row: db281878's depth.zig Rule.budgets. Off, f212's
rule prices the head's steps by the deepest chain (allocateDrafts with HeadCost, fixedMs) and
adds probeShared's row, which asks fewer drafts a stream as streams grow.

pooled_budgets_test: 4 and 16 fresh streams get db281878's numbers (3 and 2 each) pooled, and
f212's (2 and 1) unpooled, at a 6 ms head step.
